http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon-noB79L\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\" tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p></p><p>Going back even futher, you realize the return you faced for investing in gold depends a LOT on what currency you \u2018priced\u2019 your dollars in.  </p><p>Are you thinking about the price of gold in dollars, or the price of gold in yen, yuan or euro?</p><p>The reason gold spikes in the chart above in 1862 is because of the Civil War.  </p><p>The value of gold in British Pounds (\u201cGBP\u201d) didn\u2019t change in 1862, the value of the dollar did!  It went down a ton relative to both GBP and gold, and so on our chart that looks like gold going up!</p><p>Wars are bad for currencies.</p><p>In the chart below you can see our stitched together representation of the performance of gold in \u201cdollar\u201d terms, when you use a basket of colonial currencies to represent the dollar during the American Revolution. </p><p></p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image